  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Strikethrough Replace\n\nA strike line is drawn through the old text, then the new text fades in: an editorial correction.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Showing a problem being replaced by a solution: the strike says it is crossed out on purpose.\n- A pricing or comparison beat needs the old value visibly struck out before the new one appears.\n- You want editorial correction grammar: old thinking struck through, new thinking revealed.\n\nAvoid when:\n- There is no old text to cross out and you just need an entrance: use staggered-fade-up or soft-blur-in.\n- The swap should feel smooth and spatial rather than editorial: use shared-axis-y or shared-axis-z.\n- Both strings are long: the struck line gets hard to read.\n\nVariables:\n- from_text (string): From text, default \"$49/mo\"\n- to_text (string): To text, default \"Free\"\n- line_color (color): Line color, default \"#ff5e3a\"\n- font_size (number, 12-220): Font size, default 96\n- color (color): Color, default \"#171717\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"700\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Strikethrough Replace\n\n  Draws a strike line through the old text, then fades the new text in beneath it for an editorial correction.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/strikethrough-replace/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"strikethrough-replace\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"4\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"from_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"From text\", \"description\": \"Old text that gets struck out.\", \"default\": \"$49/mo\"},\n    {\"id\": \"to_text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"To text\", \"description\": \"New text that replaces it.\", \"default\": \"Free\"},\n    {\"id\": \"line_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Line color\", \"description\": \"Color of the strike line.\", \"default\": \"#ff5e3a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. Longer text shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 96, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 220, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#171717\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"700\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Strikethrough Replace</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n          color: var(--color, #171717);\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif);\n        }\n        .str-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .str-wrap { position: relative; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .str-text { letter-spacing: -0.03em; white-space: nowrap; line-height: 1.2; }\n        .str-from { position: absolute; }\n        .str-line { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 50%; width: 0; background: var(--line-color, #ff5e3a); border-radius: 2px; transform: translateY(-50%); }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"strikethrough-replace\" data-duration=\"4\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"str-clip\" class=\"str-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"4\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div class=\"str-wrap\">\n            <span id=\"str-from\" class=\"str-text str-from\" role=\"img\"></span>\n            <span id=\"str-to\" class=\"str-text\" role=\"img\"></span>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            // Easing.bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) as a function of t (Newton, then bisection).\n            function bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              function cx(s) { return 3 * x1 * s * (1 - s) * (1 - s) + 3 * x2 * s * s * (1 - s) + s * s * s; }\n              function cy(s) { return 3 * y1 * s * (1 - s) * (1 - s) + 3 * y2 * s * s * (1 - s) + s * s * s; }\n              return function (t) {\n                if (t <= 0) return 0;\n                if (t >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, s = t;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 40; i++) {\n                  var x = cx(s);\n                  if (Math.abs(x - t) < 1e-6) break;\n                  if (x < t) lo = s; else hi = s;\n                  s = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                return cy(s);\n              };\n            }\n            // interpolate(f, [a, b], [from, to]) with both ends clamped, like the source framework's extrapolate \"clamp\".\n            function interp(f, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var t = b === a ? 1 : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (f - a) / (b - a)));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(t) : t);\n            }\n            // Fit one line to 90 % of the frame width: shrinks the font size when it overflows.\n            function fit(root, line, size) {\n              line.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxWidth = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * 0.9);\n              if (line.scrollWidth > maxWidth) {\n                size = Math.max(12, size * (maxWidth / line.scrollWidth));\n                line.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            // Drives draw(frame) from the paused timeline: frame = time * 30 * speed (the source framework's useCurrentFrame() * speed).\n            function drive(tl, total, speed, draw) {\n              var clock = { t: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { t: total, duration: total, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.t * 30 * speed); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n            var fromText = str(vars.from_text, \"$49/mo\");\n            var toText = str(vars.to_text, \"Free\");\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var weight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"700\");\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--color\", vars.color);\n            if (typeof vars.line_color === \"string\" && vars.line_color) root.style.setProperty(\"--line-color\", vars.line_color);\n            var fromEl = document.getElementById(\"str-from\");\n            var toEl = document.getElementById(\"str-to\");\n            [fromEl, toEl].forEach(function (el) { el.style.fontWeight = weight; });\n            fromEl.textContent = fromText;\n            toEl.textContent = toText;\n            fromEl.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", fromText);\n            toEl.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", toText);\n            var strike = document.createElement(\"span\");\n            strike.id = \"str-strike\";\n            strike.className = \"str-line\";\n            strike.setAttribute(\"aria-hidden\", \"true\");\n            fromEl.appendChild(strike);\n\n            // Both strings share one size: shrink so the wider fits 90 % of the frame width.\n            var size = num(vars.font_size, 96, 12, 220);\n            fromEl.style.fontSize = toEl.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n            var widest = Math.max(fromEl.scrollWidth, toEl.scrollWidth);\n            var maxWidth = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * 0.9);\n            if (widest > maxWidth) {\n              size = Math.max(12, size * (maxWidth / widest));\n              fromEl.style.fontSize = toEl.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n            }\n            strike.style.height = Math.max(2, Math.round(size * 0.08)) + \"px\";\n\n            // remocn phases of the whole clip: 0-40 % draw the strike, 40-60 % cross-fade, then hold.\n            var frames = total * 30;\n            function draw(frame) {\n              strike.style.width = interp(frame, 0, frames * 0.4, 0, 100) + \"%\";\n              fromEl.style.opacity = interp(frame, frames * 0.4, frames * 0.6, 1, 0);\n              toEl.style.opacity = interp(frame, frames * 0.4, frames * 0.6, 0, 1);\n              toEl.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + interp(frame, frames * 0.4, frames * 0.6, 8, 0) + \"px)\";\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            drive(tl, total, speed, draw);\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"strikethrough-replace\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
